STM32G4 SHIP (USE A GIT BRANCH !!)

1. Mechanical / physical
    Ask Fraser to solder the horizontal headers.
    Stack boards and verify physical pin alignment.

2. Power & ground (add this)
    Map motor ground vs MCU ground.
    Decide shunt reference strategy.
    Ensure ADC inputs never exceed 3.3V.

3. Pin mapping
    Identify PWM pins Shield 3.2 uses.
    Cross-reference with STM32G4 timer channels.
    Lock in:
        TIM1 → Motor A
        TIM8 → Motor B

4. SPI buses
    Identify both SPI busses.
    Decide which peripherals go where.
    Make sure they don’t collide with PWM/ADC pins.

5. Current sensing hardware
    Identify ADC pins for inline sensing.
    Decide:
        Which 2 phases per motor.
        Which OPAMPs (internal or external).

6. Software base
    Add STM32G4 driver class (cleaned).
    Get voltage mode spinning first.
    This is critical:
    Do NOT touch current sensing until both motors spin open-loop.

7. Current sensing theory
    Understand inline sensing routine.
    Validate sampling timing.
    Decide offset calibration method.

8. Software sensing
    Add inline sensing STM32G4 subclass.
    Log raw ADC first (no FOC yet).

9. Integration
    Add inline sensing to main script.
    Enable current limits.
    Only then close Id/Iq loops.


